<title>SOUTH AFRICA: PPC yr shr flat, div up slightly.</title>
<headline>PPC yr shr flat, div up slightly.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended September 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     464.8	 vs 464.8</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 290.0	 vs 285.0</p>
<p>After tax profit</p>
<p>    - pre exceps	    200.1	 vs 194.7</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   285.8	 vs 256.5</p>
<p>    Tax			 92.0	  vs 95.4</p>
<p>    Interest received     17.1	  vs 21.5</p>
<p>    Turnover		  1,555.5     vs 1,247.6</p>
<p>Full name: Pretoria Portland Cement Company Ltd (building and construction)</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     9.4	   vs 51.7</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters forecast earnings at between 477.0 and 500.0 cents with consensus at 489.7 cents. They expected a dividend of 300 cents.</p>
<p>Directors said the exceptional items comprise a provision for closure costs.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
